_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "`round_money(2.675)` now returns `2.68`.\n\n**Cause:** the float `2.675` is actually stored as `2.67499999\u2026`. Python's built-in `round()` works on that stored value, so it rounds down. It also rounds exact halves to the nearest even digit, which doesn't match the \"half up\" promised in the docstring.\n\n**Fix** (`pricing/money.py`): `round_money` now turns the float into a `Decimal` via `repr(x)`, which gives back the number as written (`'2.675'`). It then rounds to cents with `ROUND_HALF_UP`. It still returns a `float`, so `add_vat` and other callers work as before. Negative numbers round away from zero (`-2.675 \u2192 -2.68`).\n\n**Checks:**\n- Run directly: `2.675\u21922.68`, `1.005\u21921.01`, `0.125\u21920.13`, `2.665\u21922.67`, `-2.675\u2192-2.68`, `1.234\u21921.23`. `add_vat(10.0)` gives `12.0`.\n- `test_split` passes when called directly.\n- I added `tests/test_round_money.py` with these cases. pytest isn't installed here, so I checked the same values with a plain script instead of running pytest.\n\nOne limitation: this rounds the value as written, not the exact stored float. A value that comes out of a calculation, like `2.2299999999999995`, is treated as that number and rounds to `2.23`.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 10, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 275786, "requests_cache_write": 12475, "requests_cost_usd": 0.1638602, "requests_count": 10, "requests_input_uncached": 22, "requests_output": 2312, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-bugfix-regress:claude-opus-5-5:trial2", "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 1, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-13T05:46:55.744354+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 28.952, "t_checker_s": 0.383, "t_env_setup_s